    skos:altLabel "APR"@en ;
    skos:definition "Physiological response stimulated by cytokines including interleukin-1, interleukin-6, interferons, and tumor necrosis factor (TNF), characterized by increased vascular permeability, fever, and increased levels of proteins (thus called acute-phase proteins) such as C-reactive protein (CRP), occurring within a few hours of initiation."@en ;
